From 44f020d87e88b33442b5a9fd5993db33eaa0db1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:02:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] kgsl: gen7: load the linux-firmware SQE for gen7_17_0

The gen7_17_0 core (Adreno A722, chip ID 0x43020100, Eliza) asks for
gen70e00_sqe.fw. linux-firmware does not ship that name: the A722 SQE
is published as qcom/gen71700_sqe.fw, next to the gen71700_gmu.bin
this entry already uses, and the upstream msm driver loads it under
that name. With kgsl v2.0.0 on an Eliza EVK every GPU open fails:

  kgsl-3d 3d00000.gpu: Firmware request for gen70e00_sqe.fw failed with error -2

Use gen71700_sqe.fw for gen7_17_0, following the linux-firmware naming
the newer gen7 and gen8 cores already use. No qualcomm-linux repository
ships gen70e00_sqe.fw; gen7_14_0 keeps it, since linux-firmware has
no SQE for that core.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
Upstream-Status: Pending [qualcomm-linux/kgsl, not submitted]
 adreno-gpulist.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/adreno-gpulist.h b/adreno-gpulist.h
index e446a2af..fb240016 100644
--- a/adreno-gpulist.h
+++ b/adreno-gpulist.h
@@ -2936,7 +2936,7 @@ static const struct adreno_gen7_core adreno_gpu_core_gen7_17_0 = {
 		.mal = 32,
 		.highest_bank_bit = 15,
 	},
-	.sqefw_name = "gen70e00_sqe.fw",
+	.sqefw_name = "gen71700_sqe.fw",
 	.gmufw_name = "gen71700_gmu.bin",
 	.zap_name = "gen70e00_zap.mbn",
 	.hwcg = gen7_0_0_hwcg_regs,
-- 
2.43.0

